  "body": "In https://github.com/w3c/web-nfc/issues/27#issuecomment-122013007 @domenic says \"Id\" should only have an initial capital. @annevk points out in https://github.com/jyasskin/web-bluetooth-1/commit/8154c44f9857336bb5f1d93a0aadfa3a1c19dc12#commitcomment-12208486 that I changed it the other way. https://github.com/w3ctag/design-principles/issues/15 doesn't have explicit guidance for this yet. We could avoid this by just giving `BluetoothDevice`s \"id\"s instead of \"instanceId/D\"s.\n",
